{"resource":{"id":"computer-networks-complete-tutorial","title":"Computer Networks — Complete Tutorial","category":"CS Core","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"47 min","pages":107,"lastUpdated":"May 2026","tags":["Networks","TCP/IP","CS Core"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Beginner-to-advanced Computer Networks tutorial: OSI, TCP/IP, IPv4, IPv6, routing, switching, VLANs, NAT, DNS, DHCP, HTTP/HTTPS, TCP, UDP, firewalls, VPNs, wireless, cloud networking, security, monitoring, troubleshooting."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"intro","label":"Introduction"},{"id":"osi","label":"OSI Model"},{"id":"tcpip","label":"TCP/IP Suite"},{"id":"ipv4","label":"IPv4"},{"id":"ipv6","label":"IPv6"},{"id":"routing","label":"Routing Protocols"},{"id":"switching","label":"Switching"},{"id":"vlan","label":"VLANs"},{"id":"nat","label":"NAT"},{"id":"dns","label":"DNS & DHCP"},{"id":"http","label":"HTTP/HTTPS"},{"id":"tcpudp","label":"TCP & UDP"},{"id":"firewalls","label":"Firewalls & VPNs"},{"id":"wireless","label":"Wireless Networks"},{"id":"cloud","label":"Cloud Networking"},{"id":"security","label":"Network Security"},{"id":"monitor","label":"Monitoring & Troubleshooting"},{"id":"compare","label":"Comparison Table"},{"id":"commands","label":"Commands & Code Reference"},{"id":"best","label":"Best Practices & Tips"},{"id":"mistakes","label":"Common Mistakes"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary & Key Takeaways"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"Further Reading & References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Computer Networks — Complete Tutorial","tag":"CS Core","time":"47 min"},{"title":"Computer Networks — Cheat Sheet","tag":"CS Core","time":"5 min"},{"title":"Computer Networks — Interview Questions","tag":"CS Core","time":"43 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Master the core ideas covered in this resource.</li>\n          <li>Apply concepts to hands-on labs and real networks.</li>\n          <li>Ready you for interviews and certifications.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"intro\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Introduction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Beginner-to-advanced Computer Networks tutorial: OSI, TCP/IP, IPv4, IPv6, routing, switching, VLANs, NAT, DNS, DHCP, HTTP/HTTPS, TCP, UDP, firewalls, VPNs, wireless, cloud networking, security, monitoring, troubleshooting.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Overview illustration for Computer Networks — Complete Tutorial.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"osi\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">OSI Model</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Deep-dive across all 7 layers with example protocols at each layer and how encapsulation works.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"tcpip\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">TCP/IP Suite</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Practical model. Encapsulation from application data → segment → packet → frame → bits.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Reference diagram for tcp/ip suite.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ipv4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">IPv4</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Address classes, private ranges, subnetting math, CIDR, ARP resolution.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"ipv6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">IPv6</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>128-bit addressing, SLAAC, dual-stack deployment, transition mechanisms.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"routing\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Routing Protocols</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Distance vector vs link state. RIP, OSPF, EIGRP, BGP. Convergence, metrics, admin distance.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"switching\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Switching</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>MAC learning, forwarding, filtering. STP, RSTP. Trunking with 802.1Q.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"vlan\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">VLANs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Segment broadcast domains. Access vs trunk ports. Inter-VLAN routing.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"nat\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">NAT</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Static, dynamic, PAT. Solves IPv4 exhaustion. Complications for peer-to-peer.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"dns\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">DNS &amp; DHCP</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Recursive vs authoritative servers. Record types A, AAAA, MX, CNAME, TXT. DHCP DORA process.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"http\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">HTTP/HTTPS</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Request/response, methods, status codes, headers. TLS handshake in HTTPS.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"tcpudp\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">TCP &amp; UDP</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>3-way handshake, flow control, congestion control. UDP simplicity. Port numbers.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"firewalls\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Firewalls &amp; VPNs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Stateful vs stateless. NGFWs. Site-to-site and remote access VPNs. IPsec, SSL/TLS.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"wireless\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Wireless Networks</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Wi-Fi standards, channels, security, controller-based deployments.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"cloud\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Cloud Networking</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>VPCs, subnets, security groups, transit gateways, peering, hybrid connectivity.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"security\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Network Security</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Segmentation, IDS/IPS, DDoS mitigation, Zero Trust.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"monitor\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Monitoring &amp; Troubleshooting</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>SNMP, NetFlow, syslog, Wireshark, ping/traceroute/nslookup.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"compare\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Comparison Table</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Aspect</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">TCP</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">UDP</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Reliability</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Guaranteed</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Best-effort</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Ordering</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Yes</td><td class=\"border p-2\">No</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Overhead</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Higher</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Lower</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Use cases</td><td class=\"border p-2\">HTTP, SSH, email</td><td class=\"border p-2\">DNS, VoIP, gaming</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Protocol behavior at a glance.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"commands\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Commands &amp; Code Reference</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>! Cisco IOS — VLAN + trunk basics\nvlan 10\n name USERS\nvlan 20\n name VOICE\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/1\n switchport mode access\n switchport access vlan 10\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/24\n switchport mode trunk\n switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"best\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Best Practices &amp; Tips</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Baseline before you optimize.</li>\n          <li>Document intent, not just configs.</li>\n          <li>Automate repetitive changes.</li>\n          <li>Segment aggressively; deny by default.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mistakes\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Overlapping subnets across sites.</li>\n          <li>Trunks allowing all VLANs.</li>\n          <li>Skipping change reviews.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Layered thinking, clean IP planning, and disciplined operations turn a network from fragile to boring — in the best way.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>How is this different from a general IT course?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">This resource focuses purely on networking concepts and their application.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need Cisco hardware?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No — Packet Tracer and GNS3 emulate everything you need.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is content current?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes — reflects modern protocols and enterprise practices as of May 2026.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational content. Vendor commands and versions may change — always verify against current documentation.</p>\n      </div></section>"}